-- s 9(1)(a) "does not exceed" / (b) "exceeds": the relevant amount itself is on the MAY side.
-- "specified person" (b)(i) is "below 21 years of age": 20 is, 21 is not.
-- s 9(6)(a) "before or within 7 days after the commencement": day 7 is in time, day 8 is not.
-- s 9(6)(c) needs cancellation AND a certificate dealing; cancellation alone does not bar.
-- s 9(8): a declaration does not help the insurer against earlier proceedings unless it warned the claimant within 7 days.
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment for exactly $5,000` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it may pay, but section 9 does not make it pay: the sum does not exceed the relevant amount`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment for $5,001` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment for $5,001` `a prescribed relevant amount of $20,000` EQUALS `it may pay, but section 9 does not make it pay: the sum does not exceed the relevant amount`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment for $9,000 for a 20 year old, payable to the Public Trustee` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it must pay the sum, costs and interest to the Public Trustee as trustee for the person I injured`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment for $9,000 for a 21 year old, payable to the Public Trustee` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment where my insurer never had notice` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `nothing is payable: my insurer had no notice of the proceedings within 7 days of their start`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment where my insurer had notice on day 7` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment where my insurer had notice on day 8` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `nothing is payable: my insurer had no notice of the proceedings within 7 days of their start`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment under appeal with enforcement stayed` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `nothing is payable while enforcement is stayed pending an appeal`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment after I cancelled and surrendered my certificate before the accident` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `nothing is payable: the policy was cancelled before the accident and the certificate dealt with`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment after I cancelled but kept my certificate` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment where my insurer won a declaration and warned the claimant` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `nothing is payable: the court has declared my insurer may avoid the policy`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment where my insurer won a declaration but never warned the earlier claimant` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `it must pay the sum, costs and interest directly to the person I injured`
#ASSERT `What must my insurer do about the judgment against me` `a judgment for my employee injured at work` `the relevant amount as enacted` EQUALS `section 9 does not apply to the judgment`

#ASSERT `How much can my insurer recover from me after paying under section 9` 12000 0 EQUALS 12000

§ `ss 10, 12 and 13 -- if I become bankrupt`

#ASSERT `Do my rights against my insurer pass to the person I injured` `I became bankrupt` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Do my rights against my insurer pass to the person I injured` `I became bankrupt` TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- s 12: an agreement must come after BOTH the liability and the bankruptcy; a waiver or payment only after the bankruptcy.
#ASSERT NOT `Can my dealing with my insurer after my bankruptcy defeat the injured person's rights` `a waiver, assignment, disposition, or a payment to me` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my dealing with my insurer after my bankruptcy defeat the injured person's rights` `an agreement` FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `Does my bankruptcy affect my liability to the person I injured` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my bankruptcy affect my liability to the person I injured` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 11 -- must I say whether I was insured`

`a demand where my insurer had avoided my policy and I gave no particulars` MEANS `The claimant's demand` WITH
    `a claim was made against me for a liability section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or someone for them, demanded the information` IS TRUE
    `I was insured for that liability` IS FALSE
    `I would have been insured had my insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy` IS TRUE
    `I said whether I was insured` IS TRUE
    `I gave the particulars on the certificate` IS FALSE
    `I wilfully made a false or misleading statement` IS FALSE
    `I had a reasonable excuse` IS FALSE

`the same demand, with a reasonable excuse` MEANS `The claimant's demand` WITH
    `a claim was made against me for a liability section 4(1)(b) requires to be covered` IS TRUE
    `the claimant, or someone for them, demanded the information` IS TRUE
    `I was insured for that liability` IS FALSE
    `I would have been insured had my insurer not avoided or cancelled the policy` IS TRUE
    `I said whether I was insured` IS TRUE
    `I gave the particulars on the certificate` IS FALSE
    `I wilfully made a false or misleading statement` IS FALSE
    `I had a reasonable excuse` IS TRUE

-- "or would have been so insured if the insurer had not avoided or cancelled the policy": avoidance does not end the duty.
#ASSERT `What must I tell the person claiming against me` `a demand where my insurer had avoided my policy and I gave no particulars` EQUALS `whether I was insured, and the particulars on the certificate of insurance`

#ASSERT `Am I guilty of an offence under section 11` `a demand where my insurer had avoided my policy and I gave no particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I guilty of an offence under section 11` `the same demand, with a reasonable excuse`

§ `s 15 -- surrendering my certificate`

-- "within 7 days from the taking effect of the cancellation": day 7 is in time.
#ASSERT NOT `Have I failed to surrender my certificate in time` TRUE (JUST 7)
#ASSERT `Have I failed to surrender my certificate in time` TRUE (JUST 8)

§ `s 16 -- producing my certificate and reporting an injury accident`

`stopped, details given, certificate produced at the station on day 5` MEANS `The police request` WITH
    `I was driving on a road and a police officer required it` IS TRUE
    `I gave my name and address and the owner's` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate to the officer` IS FALSE
    `days after the request that I produced it at a police station I named` IS (JUST 5)

`stopped, details given, certificate produced at the station on day 6` MEANS `The police request` WITH
    `I was driving on a road and a police officer required it` IS TRUE
    `I gave my name and address and the owner's` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate to the officer` IS FALSE
    `days after the request that I produced it at a police station I named` IS (JUST 6)

`stopped, certificate shown but the owner's details refused` MEANS `The police request` WITH
    `I was driving on a road and a police officer required it` IS TRUE
    `I gave my name and address and the owner's` IS FALSE
    `I produced my certificate to the officer` IS TRUE
    `days after the request that I produced it at a police station I named` IS NOTHING

-- s 16(3): 5 days to produce in person at the station I named; it saves only the failure to PRODUCE, not to give details.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I guilty of failing to give my details or produce my certificate` `stopped, details given, certificate produced at the station on day 5`
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of failing to give my details or produce my certificate` `stopped, details given, certificate produced at the station on day 6`
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of failing to give my details or produce my certificate` `stopped, certificate shown but the owner's details refused`

`an injury accident reported at hour 20, certificate produced on day 4` MEANS `The injury accident` WITH
    `the accident involved personal injury to another person` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate at the time to a police officer or someone entitled to ask` IS FALSE
    `hours after the accident that I reported it at a police station` IS (JUST 20)
    `the court accepts I reported as soon as possible` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate when I reported` IS FALSE
    `days after the accident that I produced it at a police station I named` IS (JUST 4)

`an injury accident reported at hour 25` MEANS `The injury accident` WITH
    `the accident involved personal injury to another person` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate at the time to a police officer or someone entitled to ask` IS FALSE
    `hours after the accident that I reported it at a police station` IS (JUST 25)
    `the court accepts I reported as soon as possible` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate when I reported` IS TRUE
    `days after the accident that I produced it at a police station I named` IS NOTHING

`an injury accident where I showed my certificate at the scene` MEANS `The injury accident` WITH
    `the accident involved personal injury to another person` IS TRUE
    `I produced my certificate at the time to a police officer or someone entitled to ask` IS TRUE
    `hours after the accident that I reported it at a police station` IS NOTHING
    `the court accepts I reported as soon as possible` IS FALSE
    `I produced my certificate when I reported` IS FALSE
    `days after the accident that I produced it at a police station I named` IS NOTHING

-- s 16(4): "in any case within 24 hours"; s 16(6): 5 days to produce. No duty if I produced it at the scene.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I guilty of failing to report the accident` `an injury accident reported at hour 20, certificate produced on day 4`
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of failing to report the accident` `an injury accident reported at hour 25`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I guilty of failing to report the accident` `an injury accident where I showed my certificate at the scene`

-- The two duties as regulative rules: a surrender on day 5 meets s 15; a report at hour 30 misses s 16(4).
#TRACE `my duty to surrender my certificate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the holder of the certificate` DOES `surrender the certificate, or declare it lost or destroyed` AT 5

#TRACE `my duty to report the accident` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the driver` DOES `report the accident at a police station and produce the certificate` AT 30

§ `penalties`

-- s 3(2): $1,000 or 3 months or both, first time. s 15(2): $500 first; $1,000 or 6 months on a second conviction.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined in dollars` `using or permitting use without cover (section 3)` FALSE EQUALS 1000

#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` `failing to surrender my certificate (section 15)` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` `failing to surrender my certificate (section 15)` TRUE EQUALS 6

